        "about": {
          "name": "Chronicle",
          "description": "Chronicle is a cancer-care lifecycle platform for patients, caregivers, care teams, and health-system leaders. A care lifecycle engine runs the stage state machine (1 → 7B with loops) from screening through treatment, response, survivorship, and relapse-driven restart, with clinician-confirmed transitions and a discussed-with-patient visibility gate. A shared patient record tracks provenance and verification for every item; documents are AI-extracted and human-confirmed; enrichment requests fill gaps against the Challenge 10 frame contract. Patients log treatment, symptoms, check-ins and wearable data and get endorsed answers with safety triage; clinicians verify records, build plans and check guideline concordance; leaders use risk-adjusted Insights and a display-only Cohort Explorer. External Python services (Aggregate Layer, ML, Metrics) and EHR are called through clients with mock modes. Analytics run as Postgres views; YAML rules and policies load as seed data. Synthetic data only; persistent notice: “Not medical advice. Discuss with your care team.”"
        },
